multiple arguments can be passed via enclosing the args on the LHS in a function call

```r
as_lambda(c(x,y) ~ x + y + 5)(x = 7, y = 2)
```

if the LHS is omitted the function is constructed identically to `as_function`. To use in place of e.g. `purrr:::as_mapper.default`, I extended `as_closure` to optionally use `as_lambda` instead of `as_function`.

