In rlang/src/lib/attrs.c r_push_attribute(x,tag,value) is used to add an attribute called
'tag' with value 'value' to the object 'x'.  It works by getting the pairlist, attrs, of tagged attributes
of x from ATTRIB(x), adding the new attribute value to the pairlist, calling SET_ATTRIB(x,attrs),
and finally adding the tag.

If it added the tag before calling SET_ATTRIB then SET_ATTRIB could do a bit of error checking
and caching based on the name of the new attribute.  (TERR does some caching for certain
attributes, like names, but R does not yet.)  It also seems wrong to have a nameless attribute,
even for a short time.

Here is a change that doesn't seem to cause any problems, but perhaps you had a good
reason for naming the attribute after it was attached to the object.

-Bill Dunlap

